{"n": 722, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "722.webp", "text": "36-4\n\nSecure a steel cable on the rear towing eye to\nhold the car.\n\nThis cable must not be drawn tight because\nof possible wrong test readings.\n\nBegip balancing on the front wheels.\n\nConnect leads for test sender.\nConform with operating instructions supplied\nwith the equipment.\n\nPaste a strip of adhesive tape or make a chalk\nmark, both 3 to 4 cm (1.181 to 1.575\") long,\non the outside of the tire being balanced,\nopposite the valve.\n\n3036055\n\nAdjust the finish balancer to correct sensitivity\n(to opersting instructions) prior to balancing.\nSince the degree of sensitivity for the balancing\nof » wheel cannot be transfered to a different\nwheel or even a different car, it must be deter\nmined separately for each wheel.\n\nBalance with engine power in fourth gear at\n100 km/h (60 mph).\n\nThis requires a smooth running engine without\nmisfiring, closed doors, engine hood and trunk\nlid and a driver sitting as quietly as possible in\nthe car.\n\nThe exhaust extraction hose must not touch\nthe tail panel.\n\nStop the wheels carefully after testing.\nRepeat test, after mounting balance weights\nat the displayed positions.\n\n{f a value of more than 15 grams is displayed\nfor a finish balanced wheel, the possible\ncauses (e.g. inaccurate stationary balancing)\nmust be eliminated and the finished wheels\nrechecked.", "words": [["36-4", 0.4666, 0.0325, 0.5218, 0.0564], ["Secure", 0.2665, 0.0729, 0.2984, 0.0836], ["a", 0.3014, 0.0756, 0.307, 0.0836], ["steel", 0.31, 0.0736, 0.3308, 0.0836], ["cable", 0.3343, 0.0736, 0.3587, 0.0836], ["on", 0.3617, 0.0756, 0.3739, 0.0836], ["the", 0.3774, 0.0736, 0.3921, 0.0836], ["rear", 0.3961, 0.0763, 0.4134, 0.0836], ["towing", 0.4174, 0.0756, 0.4493, 0.0862], ["eye", 0.4529, 0.0769, 0.4691, 0.0862], ["to", 0.4726, 0.0756, 0.4818, 0.0842], ["hold", 0.2665, 0.0889, 0.2877, 0.0995], ["the", 0.2913, 0.0889, 0.3065, 0.0995], ["car.", 0.31, 0.0915, 0.3267, 0.0995],